WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.980
What's included in the four minutes or so
of new footage added to Spider-Man: Far from

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.980
Home?

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.790
Join us as we break down what's new for the
re-release, why it might have been excluded

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:13.770
from the original cut of the film, and whether
you ought to make another trip to the theater

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.760
for it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.160
As Peter and Ned are leaving school after
finishing up their classes for the year, Peter

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.960
rattles off a list of things he has to get
done before the students leave on their European

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.920
trip.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.270
First on his list: pick up his passport from
the post office.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.570
When Peter gets there, he finds himself at
the end of a ridiculously long line, which

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.840
isn't moving at all.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.451
Anxious to move on to the rest of his tasks,
Peter unleashes a small spider-shaped drone

00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:41.770
from his backpack, which sneaks behind the
counter and opens up another passport pickup

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:46.120
line, which had been closed so that the postal
worker behind the glass could eat lunch.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.860
It's not really necessary to understand the
rest of the film, but it's a clever little

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.290
bit of foreshadowing.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:55.730
He needs a passport to travel abroad, and
his use of a drone is a small-scale version

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.840
how Quentin Beck will later use drones for
his master plan.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.760
As part of his plan to woo MJ in Europe, Peter
wants to buy her a glass Black Dahlia necklace

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:08.179
in Venice, after which he'll give it to her
at the top of the Eiffel Tower.

00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:12.799
The only problem is, he doesn't actually have
enough money to get the necklace, so he says

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:16.850
goodbye to a few prized possessions in pursuit
of some quick cash.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.600
Peter heads to a pawn shop, carrying a box
of superhero action figures.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.459
"Those are collectible action figures, and
they're worth more than your car!"

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:28.229
Although the camera only lingers on the box
for a second, making it difficult to tell

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:33.090
exactly which characters it contains, there
is one that Peter decides at the last second

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.249
not to pawn.

00:01:34.249 --> 00:01:38.420
Plucking what appears to be a mostly yellow
figure from the box, Peter tells the pawn

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.749
shop owner that he's decided to keep "the
robot" after all.

00:01:41.749 --> 00:01:46.079
This could be a nod to Peter's deep attachment
to Tony Stark, a man who essentially dressed

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:47.079
as a robot.

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:49.509
Or it could be someone we've never seen before.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:53.689
If Sony and Marvel have really parted ways
for future Spidey films, it's questionable

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:57.819
whether any of the seed planting in Far from
Home will ever come to fruition.

00:01:57.819 --> 00:02:02.409
This one likewise isn't necessary to the plot,
but it is a nice tip of the symbolic hat to

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:06.929
the fact that Far from Home marks the end
of Phase 3 of the MCU and a changing of the

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:08.160
superhero guard.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:13.070
Next, Peter stops at at his local bodega,
where he purchases the dual headphone adapter

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.590
that is so crucial to his romantic goals.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:21.030
After Peter makes a valiant but terrible attempt
to communicate what he's looking for in Spanish,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.390
the bodega owner corrects him and sells him
the adapter, telling Peter he needs to work

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.860
on his "Spanglish."

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:31.130
Of course, Peter's plan for the dual headphone
adapter to use it to watch movies on the plane

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:36.610
with MJ goes tragically sideways, and he winds
up sitting next to his teacher Mr. Harrington

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:42.100
instead, while MJ and Peter's rival Brad watch
movies using the dual adapter that Brad also

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.640
happened to have with him.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.040
The bodega scene was probably cut for a reason,
but it does drive home just how much effort

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.680
he put into getting all the pieces of his
plan to win over MJ right.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.360
Finally, just before leaving the country,
Peter takes down a local organized crime syndicate

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.690
operating out of an Italian restaurant.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.990
Wearing the Iron Spider suit that Tony gave
him in Avengers: Infinity War, Peter handily

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:09.010
dispatches a roomful of baddies while delivering
a barrage of quips about one-star Yelp reviews

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.540
and stingy tips.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.080
The police compliment Peter on his new suit,
realizing it's obviously Stark tech.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.470
"You gonna be the next Iron Man now?"

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.470
"Well, no, I don't have time.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.640
I'm too busy doing your job."

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.640
"Ohhhh!"

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.980
"I'm kidding, I'm kidding!"

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:24.990
It's one of many reminders we get in Far from
Home that Peter is still grieving the loss

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.810
of Tony, a mental state that Beck takes full
advantage of.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.110
It's a fun Spidey action sequence, but given
that there's no shortage of action and Tony

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.440
Stark reminders in Far from Home, it's easy
to understand why it didn't make the final

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.200
cut.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.280
After Mysterio assumes he has killed Spider-Man,
he turns his sights to the other loose threads

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.020
in his plan Ned, MJ, and Betty.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.569
He decides to stage a massive attack in London,
in which Mysterio will save the city from

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:55.380
an "Avengers-level threat," but not before
there are extensive civilian casualties, Peter's

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.490
friends included.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:01.120
Beck gathers a group of his accomplices together
in a parking garage and reminds them to make

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.210
sure to take plenty of video and upload it
to the internet, since all the civilians who

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.209
would normally be posting to social media
will be dead.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:12.600
After all, if Mysterio is going to be the
next Iron Man, he's going to have to go viral.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:17.190
He then takes a call from Nick Fury, who informs
him of an Elemental threat in London, which,

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.540
of course, Beck planned.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:23.520
The scene ends with Beck ending the call and
repeating his earlier line: "Never apologize

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.650
for being the smartest person in the room."

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:29.439
While this scene definitely drives home just
how far Beck is willing to go for the sake

00:04:29.439 --> 00:04:34.509
of his plan, it pushes him a little too far
into cartoonish, mustache-twirling territory,

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.560
with his casual talk of dead innocents and
a catchphrase at the end.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.600
While the scenes added to the Spider-Man:
Far from Home re-release mostly consist of

00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:47.550
fun Spidey stuff, none of it really enhances
the plot or the characters in any meaningful

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.550
way.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.319
It's all pretty superfluous, and in the case
of the Mysterio scene, may actually work to

00:04:52.319 --> 00:04:53.779
the film's detriment.

00:04:53.779 --> 00:04:57.889
The Peter-centric scenes are entertaining,
and the restaurant fight is a great opportunity

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.370
to see the Iron Spider suit in action one
last time.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.780
Whether it's worth a return to the theater
depends on how much you liked Far from Home

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.650
to begin with, since it's basically the same
movie.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:11.240
If you kind of wanted to see it again anyway,
or if you haven't managed to see it for the

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.979
first time, it's a good excuse to finally
go.

